<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.9.9: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00515</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.9.9: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b059a85d-12db-4b78-bd83-8218c113f674</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">To help students synthesize the work in this lesson, display the following prompt for all to see: “How does solving the equation \( 4x−3=12(x+3) \) help with solving the inequality \( 4x−3≥12(x+3) \)?”</para>
<para dir="ltr">Ask students to explain in their own words and in writing. If time permits, ask students to share their response with a partner, and then invite a student or two to share with the class a particularly clear explanation their partner has written.</para>
 </section>
</content>
</document>
